# Canonical Turtle for the protocol-derived encoding of:
#   Hongyu Yu et al. (2024). Physics-informed time-reversal equivariant neural network potential for magnetic materials.
#   Physical review. B./Physical review. B. doi:10.1103/physrevb.110.104427  arXiv:2211.11403v3
#
# Version read: arxiv-preprint arXiv:2211.11403v3 (sha256 b24d4d286c7aea60...);
#   the DOI above is cited, numbers are those of the version read.
# Corpus rank 634 (Method/model). Method identity follows
#   artifacts/kg/METHODS.md (registry: artifacts/kg/methods-registry.csv).
# Generated by artifacts/scripts/encode_paper.py from artifacts/kg/encoding/specs/yu2024physics.yaml.
#
# Encoding scope: the Spin-Allegro++ models introduced in the paper
# (registry method Spin-Allegro++, origin) with different spin-interaction
# terms, and spin-free Allegro baselines trained on the same data, for
# monolayer CrI3 and CrTe2 (Tables 1 and 3), plus the Spin-Allegro++ fit to
# the artificial MnGe-type spin-lattice benchmark (energy only). Magnetic
# ground states, magnetic energy differences and Curie temperatures are
# property results.

